   "title": "Trails of the Roger Pryor Pioneer Backcountry | Missouri State Parks",
   "text": "Skip to main content\nSearch\nSelect Language\nEnglish\nFrançais\nDeutsch\nItaliano\nEspañol\nPARK/SITE STATUS\nTHINGS TO DO\nMAKE A RESERVATION\nFIND YOUR PARK\nTRAILS OF THE ROGER PRYOR PIONEER BACKCOUNTRY\nACTIVITIES & ACCOMMODATIONS\nSITE INFORMATION\nSolitude reigns in the Roger Pryor Pioneer Backcountry, a 60,000-acre tract adjacent to Echo Bluff State Park. The backcountry is part of Pioneer Forest, which is owned by the L-A-D Foundation. It is Missouri's largest privately owned forest. The foundation donates its lease of the backcountry’s 70 miles of trail to the Missouri Department of Natural Resources for the enjoyment of visitors to Missouri State Parks.\nPark file\nAdvisories\nPark Hours\nPark and Site Status Map\n2026 Public Meeting\n2025 Public Meeting\nPark Trails\nArea Attractions\nPhoto Gallery\nVideo\nContact usEvents\nTab through to leave this widget\nor\nfollow this link to go back to the first tab\nMap zoom\n11\nABOUT US\nState Park Rangers\nVolunteer Opportunities\nSupport Your State Parks\nAbout the Park System\nPublic Meetings\nHistoric Preservation Office\nNatural Areas\nWild Areas\nConcession Opportunities\nJob Opportunities\nConceptual Development Plans\nStrategic Plan\nGrant Opportunities\nParks, Soils and Water Sales Tax\nDept. of Natural Resources\nOPTIMIZE YOUR EXPERIENCE\nAccessibility Information\nCamping Reservation System\nOne-Tank Trips\nState Parks Online Store\nTrip Planner\nWater Recreation Safety Tips\nEncounters With Nature\nFind a Plant or Animal\nMissouri Tourism\nTHINGS TO KNOW\nADA Information\nNon-Discrimination Notice\nPark and Site Status Map\nNew to Missouri State Parks?\nQuick List of Parks/Sites\nFacts and Figures\nNews Releases\nWhat's New\nLaws and Regulations\nPets and Parks\nAlerts and Advisories\nLinks of Interest\nContact Us\nSOCIAL TOOLBAR (FOOTER)\nEmail us\nLike us on Facebook\nFollow us on Twitter\nWatch videos on YouTube\nThe Missouri Department of Natural Resources does not endorse, make clai